t to me.<br /> <br /> There are clear, concise rules for how they work.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would go strictly against ChroD editorial mandates. If you want that sort of thing, try D&amp;D and how it gave stat blocks to deities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T14:50:27-08:00","id":1006406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1004294-invisible-entities-clash-of-wills?p=1005974#post1005974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That would go strictly against ChroD editorial mandates. If you want that sort of thing, try D&amp;D and how it gave stat blocks to deities.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dude what.<br /> <br /> Have you <i>read </i>Imperial Mysteries.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T14:56:33-08:00","id":1006411,"title":"","content":"One could solve this standoff by posting the stats and write-up for a Rank 6 or higher being.<br /> <br /> Though I think there is merit in just repeating the name of a book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T15:31:36-08:00","id":1006433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1004294-invisible-entities-clash-of-wills?p=1006411#post1006411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One could solve this standoff by posting the stats and write-up for a Rank 6 or higher being.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can post the <i>rules </i>for statting them, but the book doesn't actually give any fully statted entities themselves.<br /> <br /> Spirits, Astral entities, Supernal natives, the inhabitants of the Underworld, and other, stranger beings all use the rules for spirits (pp. 317\u2013322, Mage: The Awakening), but archmasters deal with entities of such power that they would be classed as Princes, Dukes or Kings on the spiritual hierarchy.<br /> <br /> In the manner of an archmage creating an Ochema, Spirits of rank 6 and above can create sub-selves called Royal Avatars to interact with lesser beings, which have the personality of the entire being but are only rank 5. Archmages can summon the true entity to force an appearance, but it is wiser to go to their homes and ask politely.<br /> <br /> As described on page 317 of Mage, spirits of Rank 6 and above do not have conventional traits. Assume that a god like spirit has trait maximums of 15 but achieves additional, automatic successes on any roll equal to its Rank in anything relating to its purview or its Rank \u2014 5 for anything else. Add Rank to any passive calculations such as Defense or resisting certain spells. Godlike spirits have ever-renewing supplies of Essence, having a maximum of 25 x Rank and regaining their Rank per turn. Such beings have too many Numina to list. Instead, their Influence has grown to the point that they are able to improvise Numina in the manner of a mage improvising a spell, using the following guidelines<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\" style=\"width: 500px\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><b>Level</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><b>Influence</b></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">6</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">The spirit may use any power covered by spells from the common Practices of any Arcanum, as long as the power relates to its area of influence. Convert Mana costs to Essence and add the standard one Essence for using an<br /> Influence. Extended spells must still be \u201ccast\u201d over time, each \u201croll\u201d taking half an hour.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">7</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">The spirit may use powers from the Practices of Dynamics, Excision and Entities as long as they relate to its area of infl uence. Extended spells of the common Practices may be duplicated as instant action Numina. Convert Arcane Experience and Mana costs to Essence</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">8</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">The spirit may achieve anything related to its area of influence, as though it were under the effect of the Practice of Transfiguration.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">9</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">The spirit may use Numina based on the Imperial Practices as instant actions.</td> </tr> </table></div> Some beings that use the spirit rules \u2014 Ochemata, Supernal natives and the Aeons in particular \u2014 have powers that more closely resemble magic. Instead of Infl uences, these beings have true Arcana ratings and use Mana instead of Essence. Supernal gods and the Aeons are capable of casting Imperial Spells as instant actions without Arcane Experience or Quintessence costs, while Ochemata still cast in the same manner as the archmage who created them.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-22T03:06:51-08:00","id":1006640,"title":"","content":"Those guidelines are, as you can tell by reading them, more fudgey than a fudge vat at a fudge factory. They're intended to throw storytellers a bone in deciding just how hard Dread Dormammu punches, and are not binding.<br /> <br /> Luna does not actually have Awakened magic; all the above translates to is &quot;is it to do with the moon, madness, guardianship, shapeshifting, or any of the other stuff she's the spirit of? Then she can do it.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-22T16:32:09-08:00","id":1006898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1004294-invisible-entities-clash-of-wills?p=1006640#post1006640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Those guidelines are, as you can tell by reading them, more fudgey than a fudge vat at a fudge factory. They're intended to throw storytellers a bone in deciding just how hard Dread Dormammu punches, and are not binding.<br /> <br /> Luna does not actually have Awakened magic; all the above translates to is &quot;is it to do with the moon, madness, guardianship, shapeshifting, or any of the other stuff she's the spirit of? Then she can do it.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think they make plenty of sense. There are rules for how they function and how an Archmaster can interact with them. Since I cannot find any specific mention in the book that these rules are not binding, I will assume that you are referring to Rule Zero, in which case <i>no rules</i> are binding because the Storyteller can just change them.<br /> <br /> That Luna does not in fact have Awakened magic is pretty obvious given that she doesn't <i>use Mana</i> and that it's not called an Arcanum (it's still an Influence), but that doesn't really invalidate my point, they are still <i>rules</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-22T16:54:14-08:00","id":1006905,"title":"","content":"Yes, I know. I wrote it.<br /> <br /> &quot;Not binding&quot; in that it's a 500-word kludge to approximate Royal spirits in Mage's existing mechanics. If Werewolf or Geist ever did give rules for Rank 6+ things, I would expect them to be different.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-22T18:05:21-08:00","id":1006936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1004294-invisible-entities-clash-of-wills?p=1006905#post1006905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If Werewolf or Geist ever did give rules for Rank 6+ things, I would expect them to be different.</div> </div> </div> </div>I personally wouldn't mind knowing how the fuck Gurdilag was defeated, it being a rank 6 Idigam, bane or not used against it.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-22T19:40:25-08:00","id":1006975,"title":"","content":"Army of werewolves and their totems led by 6 Max Roman and armed with its ban. Even with the new rules it doesn't seem that far-fetched.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attach