age-the-awakening/1004294-invisible-entities-clash-of-wills?p=1006977#post1006977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Devil is on the details still.</div> </div> </div> </div>It really shouldn't be. The ban extended to all the creatures it made. Max managed to unite an army of werewolves and spirits, all armed with the thing it was weak against. The details would likely just be of a long and tedious series of battles that left dead on both sides and a handful of survivors on one.<br /> <br /> The thing that's been a mystery about it is how he found that ban to begin with. It was the water from an underground lake that seems to be deep in the Hisil, and while he's obviously told people what it was and a bit about it, he's never explained how he found it and no one who went with him has either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-23T13:08:08-08:00","id":1007390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1004294-invisible-entities-clash-of-wills?p=1006905#post1006905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, I know. I wrote it.</div> </div> </div> </div>You did? I'd like to thank you for that, they were most useful in my Archmaster chronicle. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> [/QUOTE]&quot;Not binding&quot; in that it's a 500-word kludge to approximate Royal spirits in Mage's existing mechanics. If Werewolf or Geist ever did give rules for Rank 6+ things, I would expect them to be different.[/QUOTE]<br /> <br /> Naturally. <br /> <br /> Rank 6+ Spirits/Ghosts/Goetia/Angels/Whatever would be so significant that they might as well have their own book due to their impact on the world.<br /> <br /> But they're still the only precedence we have, and my lawyer training tells me that any amount of precedence is useful, since I did make a positive claim, and should therefore provide the evidence to support it. <br /> <br /> But on another note, you could pretty much do Rank 6+ Ephemeral Entities just with the core. An Influence of 9 in something would allow such a being to Mass Create Permanently, which is ridiculously powerful.<br /> <br /> Like, with Fire 9, you can arbitrarily declare that &quot;this place will burn forever&quot;, and basically nothing can stop this from happening.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}